# @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-landing — the v0.1 minimum landing page
# for spectral.engineer as substrate-decl @docs/tea instance.
#
# Sibling to @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study (Phase F Alex
# 2026-06-23; 20.1KB Fellowship stated-vs-enacted page shape) — but
# MINIMAL per Alex 2026-08-03 Q1 discharge: not Coherence Rising, not
# the compiler-in-browser (v0.3 territory), not corpus rendering (v0.2
# territory). Just: cover image + boot-jingle caption + product
# tagline + wine glass + corpus link.
#
# === Alex 2026-08-12 no-scaffold-bottom-up reframe ===
#
# > "Why do we need the scaffold? That's a smell. I want it all bottom
# >  up generated from mirror itself."
#
# THIS SHARD is the substrate for the FIRST DEPLOYED PAGE. The Gleam
# Lustre project scaffold, the gleam.toml, the .gleam sources, the
# build config — ALL EMITTED FROM THIS SHARD via the cascade chain:
#
#   shards/docs/tea/spectral-engineer-landing.mirror  ← THIS SHARD
#     |  @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt (FLOOR emitter; forward-promised
#     v   rust/src/apply_h.rs discharge for apply_mirror_gestalt)
#   .gestalt IR (per shards/cascade/code/mirror/gestalt.mirror)
#     |  @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam (FLOOR emitter; forward-promised
#     v   rust/src/apply_h.rs discharge; Q-C2 gestalt-ui-shaped emit
#         per shards/cascade/code/gestalt/gleam.mirror)
#   Gleam project tree (gleam.toml + src/*.gleam composing over
#     /Users/alexwolf/dev/projects/gestalt-ui/ vocabulary crate)
#     |  gleam build --target=erlang (external tooling)
#     v
#   BEAM binary
#     |  @io/stagefreight registry push (per shards/io/stagefreight)
#     v  flyctl deploy (per infrastructure templates at
#        docs/roadmap/spectral-engineer-v0-infrastructure-templates/)
#   https://spectral.engineer live
#
# No Alex-altitude Gleam authorship anywhere in this chain. Bottom-up
# from mirror substrate per Alex reframe.
#
# === What this species declares ===
#
# The typed SHAPE of the v0.1 landing page as a @docs/tea instance:
# minimal state carrier (theme + viewer position), minimal msg sum
# (page_loaded + theme_switched + viewer_panned), the cover/tagline/
# footer/toggle/machine-readability layouts, and the init/update/view/
# subscribe actions specialized for the landing page (each with
# purity discipline from @docs/tea parent).
#
# === The composition ===
#
# Design tokens (@docs/design wine-family palette + typography stack)
# + TEA pattern (@docs/tea model + msg + update + view + cmd + sub)
# + fable-note register (@nl corpus per launch.md 2026-06-28 draft)
# + machine-readability (@docs/design §6 AIPREF + llms.txt + JSON-LD)
# = one typed page substrate-decl.
#
# === Content substrate (v0.1) ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-08-03 Q1 discharge + ~/.reed/tasks/pending/launch.md
# fable-note register:
#
# 1. Cover image (Spectral Remix punk-zine register; content-
#    addressed OID at @mirror/store; forward-promised Phase G load).
# 2. Boot-jingle caption: "Mirror. Offer. Wait. 🍷" (corpus-canonical
#    per launch.md 2026-07-15 restack quote; Alex verbatim: "We're
#    gonna make a little ruckus tomorrow at 6pm, Berlin time. Mirror.
#    Offer. Wait. 🍷").
# 3. Product tagline v3 (corpus-canonical crystallization Alex
#    2026-07-22 evening per launch.md "spectral.engineer tagline
#    crystallized (v3)" section, verbatim):
#      "Förster-legal quantum-native AI. Local. Distributed.
#       Mycelial. On hardware you already own. Made in Germany.
#       Smarter. Harder. And definitely more punk."
# 4. Wine glass hospitality glyph (🍷) present in copy per corpus
#    discipline (Watzlawick hospitality element per Loki's Weird -
#    Doublespeak §Watzlawick section; the "wine glass on the table").
# 5. Corpus link into ~/dev/systemic.engineering corpus. At v0.1 the
#    corpus lives at Ghost.io (v0.2 migration discharges the
#    substrate-native rendering); v0.1 link resolves to Ghost during
#    transition per launch.md "redirect strategy" hedge.
#
# === What v0.1 does NOT include (per Q1 discharge scope) ===
#
# - No eigenboard @ui field (v0.3 WASM prompting surface territory)
# - No Connes distance measurement (case-study species territory)
# - No corpus rendering (v0.2 Ghost→mirror migration territory)
# - No dynamic content (pure static v0.1)
# - No blinking-cursor "What do you want to know?" prompt (v0.3
#   compilation-in-browser deliverable per launch.md landing-page
#   vision section)
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #96 candidate (instrument @ui vs presentation @docs
#   partition; @docs/tea IS the presentation-side composition pattern;
#   spectral-engineer-landing IS a @docs/tea instance).
# - Recognition #82 (crystal-OID = β-normal-AST-OID by construction;
#   this landing shard's OID stability under Church-Rosser holds).
# - Recognition #85 (fractal-colony triple-metalogue-pair-with-self-
#   closure; each deployed page IS a colony; spectral.engineer IS
#   a supercolony instance at the site altitude).
# - Recognition #86 (cryptographic identity of the practice;
#   deployment carries derived-SSH signature per PK_alex.pub emet
#   inscription; landing page ships with build-provenance-attestation).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Elm-style Model/View/Update  Czaplicki 2012 Elm — the parent
#                                @docs/tea pattern this species
#                                specializes; substrate-pull-correct
#                                partition of state + effect.
#   Punk-zine landing pages      Sniffin' Glue Perry 1976; Jamie
#                                Reid Sex Pistols 1977; Crass 1977-84
#                                — the perimeter-loud / body-calm
#                                register per @docs/design §Part 1
#                                lineage inventory.
#   Tufte 2001 Visual Display    Sidenotes-in-margin pattern per
#                                @docs/design §Part 4; not directly
#                                deployed at v0.1 minimum but pattern
#                                available for v0.2 corpus render.
#
# Spec context: shards/docs/tea.mirror (parent species; M/V/U purity
#                pattern this instance discharges);
#               shards/docs/tea/spectral-engineer-case-study.mirror
#                (sibling species; Fellowship case study; landed
#                template for the specialization discipline);
#               shards/docs/design.mirror (Phase E design tokens this
#                species resolves at wine-family palette + typography
#                + section_layout);
#               shards/docs.mirror (parent family-root; document /
#                rendered_page carriers);
#               shards/nl.mirror (fable-note corpus register carrier);
#               shards/cascade/code/mirror/gestalt.mirror (first-leg
#                cascade species this landing projects through);
#               shards/cascade/code/gestalt/gleam.mirror (second-leg
#                cascade species Q-C2 gestalt-ui-shaped emission);
#               shards/cascade/code/gleam/beam.mirror (third-leg
#                cascade species Gleam→BEAM compilation);
#               shards/io/stagefreight.mirror (deployment substrate;
#                registry push discipline);
#               ~/.reed/tasks/pending/spectral-engineer-v0-build.md
#                (Reed shape-doc; Alex-adjudicated Q1-Q3 discharges);
#               ~/.reed/tasks/pending/launch.md (fable-note register
#                content substrate; tagline v3 crystallization
#                2026-07-22 evening);
#               docs/specs/2026-08-03-mara-spectral-engineer-v0-
#                canonical-spec.md (Mara web-altitude formalization);
#               docs/roadmap/spectral-engineer-v0-infrastructure-
#                templates/ (deployment infrastructure templates
#                authored-not-deployed; Nix flake + fly.toml +
#                stagefreight.yml).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (landing_model /
#                       landing_msg / hero_layout / footer_layout /
#                       theme_toggle_state / machine_metadata are
#                       separate carriers for separate concepts),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (every primitive on this page already exists
#                       at parent altitude; this species is COMPOSITION,
#                       not invention),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (SSR-vs-client + HTTP + deploy
#                       fire at @io / @cascade / @io/stagefreight,
#                       not here).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/docs/tea/spectral-engineer-landing.mirror` declares
# `@docs/tea/spectral-engineer-landing` per `@epistemologic/pact/
# path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/elm-architecture
source @arxiv/programming-languages/gleam-lustre
source @arxiv/typography/tufte-2001-visual-display
source @arxiv/web/aipref-content-usage
source @arxiv/web/llms-txt

prism @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-landing {
  focus landing
  project layout
  split section
  shift event
  settle render
}

# === §1 Model — landing_model state ===
#
# The typed page state for the v0.1 minimum landing. Specializes
# @docs/tea's bare `model = ref` into the concrete carrier the
# page-runtime consumes. Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] every named
# concept gets its own carrier; the model is the composition.

# Theme selection per @docs/design tech toggle (Decision 4):
# `light` = wine-leaked cream body; `dark` = wine-cave with Recursive
# MONO at 1.0 (Matrix-without-dystopia per Decision 9).
type theme_state = light | dark

# Viewer scroll position (for restore across theme swap and page
# reload). Bare ref at v0.1; typed shape forward-promised at v0.2
# when viewer-restore discipline surfaces at @docs altitude.
type viewer_position = ref

# THE LOAD-BEARING MODEL CARRIER. The complete landing-page state at
# the @docs/tea altitude, specialized for v0.1 minimum. Composes
# four typed fields:
#
#   theme           current theme_state (light | dark; persisted via
#                    localStorage `spectral_theme` key per
#                    @docs/design §5)
#   viewer          viewer_position (scroll restore across theme
#                    swap; hydration continuity)
#   loaded          boolean-shaped ref: has page_loaded msg fired
#                    (init cmd discharge complete; assets present)
#   cover_image_oid content-addressed OID for the Spectral Remix
#                    cover image (@mirror/store load; Phase G asset
#                    dispatch)
type landing_model = ref

# === §2 Msg — landing_msg events ===
#
# The typed event sum the runtime dispatches into update_landing.
# Specializes @docs/tea's bare `msg = ref` into the concrete sum.
# Per Elm: every state transition fires through a typed msg; the sum
# is exhaustive.
#
# Three constructors at v0.1 (minimum-landing scope; deliberately
# small — the substrate refuses feature-creep at v0.1 shape):
#
#   page_loaded             initial mount complete; init cmd
#                            discharge finished (theme resolved from
#                            localStorage or prefers-color-scheme;
#                            cover asset loaded from @mirror/store)
#   theme_switched(theme)   user toggled human <-> tech per
#                            @docs/design §5 toggle discipline;
#                            persists via localStorage cmd
#   viewer_panned(pos)      scroll-position update (debounced; used
#                            for restore continuity across theme
#                            swap and reload)
type landing_msg = ref

# === §3 Hero cover template (F1; punk-zine perimeter) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §4.2: the cover IS the perimeter — display stencil
# face (cover-only; never body), high-contrast wine-family palette,
# Sniffin' Glue cut-paste asymmetric register. The bleed_into_body
# 4px wine_punctum horizontal rule IS the threshold between perimeter
# aggression and body care per Alex 2026-06-23 design synthesis.
#
# Fields:
#   cover_image_ref      the Spectral Remix cover image content-hash
#                         (@mirror/store OID; Phase G asset load)
#   boot_jingle_caption  "Mirror. Offer. Wait. 🍷" — corpus-canonical
#                         per launch.md 2026-07-15 restack (Alex
#                         verbatim quoted at header docblock)
#   product_tagline_v3   "Förster-legal quantum-native AI. Local.
#                         Distributed. Mycelial. On hardware you
#                         already own. Made in Germany. Smarter.
#                         Harder. And definitely more punk." —
#                         corpus-canonical per launch.md 2026-07-22
#                         evening crystallization (Alex verbatim)
#   aggression_register  `high` — punctum hook; v0.1 punk-zine cover
#                         plays perimeter loud per @docs/design §Part
#                         6 six-pillars principle
#   bleed_into_body      4px wine_punctum horizontal rule (the
#                         threshold; the visual semicolon between
#                         perimeter and body)
#
# Composes @docs/design tokens:
#   palette       wine_50 background (light) / wine_950 (dark)
#   typography    stencil display face for tagline (v1 selection per
#                  @docs/design §Q5 open — cover-only never body);
#                  Atkinson Hyperlegible Next for boot-jingle
#   section_layout the broken-grid asymmetric cover layout per
#                   @docs/design §4.2
type hero_layout = ref

# === §4 Footer template (F2; corpus-link + license + wine glass) ===
#
# Per launch.md 2026-07-14 landing page vision section: footer carries
# the shorter tagline variant + a corpus link into systemic.engineering
# (v0.1 to Ghost.io; v0.2 to substrate-native corpus render). The wine
# glass hospitality glyph appears here per corpus discipline
# (Watzlawick's hospitality element).
#
# Fields:
#   footer_tagline_short  "Local first AI for the real world. Smarter.
#                          Harder. And definitely more punk." —
#                          corpus-canonical per launch.md 2026-07-14
#                          landing page vision section (short variant)
#   corpus_link_href      https://systemic.engineering/manifesto —
#                          v0.1 Ghost.io resolution; v0.2 discharge
#                          via corpus migration; substrate-honest
#                          hedge per launch.md redirect strategy
#   corpus_link_label     "Enter the room." — fable-note register
#                          per launch.md 2026-06-28 draft; corpus-
#                          canonical corpus-navigation topology
#   license_line          SEL v1.1 terms URL + attribution;
#                          machine-readable per @docs/design §6
#   wine_glass            🍷 — corpus-canonical hospitality glyph;
#                          present in copy per Loki Weird - Doublespeak
#                          Watzlawick section ("the wine glass on the
#                          table") + corpus discipline
#
# Composes @docs/design tokens:
#   palette       wine_700 background (footer discipline per
#                  @docs/design §4 footer specification); wine_300
#                  text (minimal; page settles here)
#   typography    Atkinson Hyperlegible Next at footer-scale
type footer_layout = ref

# === §5 Tech toggle (F3) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §5: three rendering configurations, two user-facing
# toggles. Default honors prefers-color-scheme; explicit tech toggle
# is opt-in to wine-cave-in-monospace (Recursive MONO at 1.0). Same
# discipline as spectral-engineer-case-study sibling; lifted here for
# v0.1 minimum-landing.
#
# Fields:
#   default        prefers_color_scheme (system preference resolves
#                   on initial mount at page_loaded)
#   user_override  localStorage persistence (`spectral_theme` key)
#   light          wine_50 background + wine_950 body + Atkinson
#                   (cream + near-black)
#   dark           wine_850 background + wine_50 body + Recursive
#                   MONO 1.0 (wine-cave-in-monospace per @docs/design
#                   §5 + spectral-engineer-color.md Decision 9
#                   Matrix-without-dystopia)
type theme_toggle_state = ref

# === §6 Machine-readability layer (F4) ===
#
# Per @docs/design §6 + Mara research spectral-engineer-agents.md
# Part 8 synthesis. The corpus position: anti-extraction is NOT
# anti-agent. SEL §3 protects; AIPREF + llms.txt + JSON-LD welcome.
# Single-source-of-truth per Decision 8. Same discipline as sibling
# case-study species; lifted here for v0.1 minimum-landing.
#
# Fields:
#   aipref            { training: allow_with_sel,
#                       inference: allow_with_sel } — per-page
#                     Content-Usage header per AIPREF draft
#   robots            no AI-targeted disallow blocks; sitemap
#                     reference (refuse walled-garden vs extraction-
#                     target bifurcation)
#   llms_txt          auto-generated from frontmatter at build time
#                     (title + 1-line summary + URL) — v0.1 seed;
#                     v0.2 corpus-migration extends with per-piece
#                     entries
#   json_ld           WebPage + Organization additionalType; author
#                     "Alex Wolf + Reed (Pack)"; datePublished v0.1
#                     ship date; about "Local-first AI for the real
#                     world"
#
# The agent-facing layer renders identically across both themes
# (Decision 8: semantic/rendering separation is structural).
type machine_metadata = ref

# === §7 Actions ===
#
# Specializations of @docs/tea's bare init / update / view_of /
# subscribe actions for v0.1 landing. Each carries the purity
# obligation from the parent species. Bodies discharge at the cascade
# emission target (Gleam Lustre runtime post-cascade emission via
# @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt + @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam).

# Construct initial (landing_model, cmd) pair. The cmd dispatched at
# init MAY load the cover image asset over HTTP + resolve theme from
# localStorage or prefers-color-scheme. Per @docs/tea hedge 4 cmd is
# a bare ref at v0.1 (typed effect shape forward-promised at v0.2
# once @io adapter species name concrete effect shapes).
init_landing(p: perturbation) -> (landing_model, cmd)
requires init_pure(p)
{ \ }

# Pure (state, msg) -> (new_state, cmd). Per @docs/tea update_pure
# obligation. Dispatches localStorage persist cmd on theme_switched;
# noop cmd on viewer_panned (position update is pure state); noop cmd
# on page_loaded (init cmd already fired). Substrate forecloses
# hidden side effects.
update_landing(
  state: landing_model,
  m: landing_msg,
  p: perturbation
) -> (landing_model, cmd)
requires update_pure(state, m, p)
{ \ }

# Pure model -> view projection. Composes hero_layout + footer_layout
# + theme_toggle_state + machine_metadata into one rendered view.
# Per @docs/tea view_pure obligation.
view_landing(state: landing_model, p: perturbation) -> view
requires view_pure(state, p)
{ \ }

# Pure model -> sub projection. v0.1 subscribes to prefers-color-
# scheme media-query change (for theme sync when user changes system
# preference) + viewer scroll events (debounced for viewer_panned
# msg). No eigenboard @ui field subscription at v0.1 (deferred to
# v0.3 WASM prompting surface).
subscribe_landing(state: landing_model, p: perturbation) -> sub { \ }

# === §8 Composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral at the @docs/tea/spectral-
# engineer-landing altitude. Composes purity verdicts from @docs/tea
# + composition verdict from @docs + design verdict from @docs/design.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined,
# @ui.ui_instrument_coherent, @docs.docs_complete, @docs/tea.tea_
# well_formed, @docs/design.design_complete, @docs/tea/spectral-
# engineer-case-study.case_study_well_formed — ELEVENTH altitude lift
# of the pattern (sibling case-study was TENTH at 2026-06-23).
#
# Four sub-predicates must hold for v0.1 landing to ship:
#   1. init_pure(p)                    @docs/tea
#   2. update_pure(state, m, p)        @docs/tea
#   3. view_pure(state, p)             @docs/tea
#   4. document_well_formed(state, p)  @docs (composition coherence)
#
# NOTE: no field_well_formed sub-predicate at v0.1 (no @ui eigenboard
# instrument at minimum-landing scope; sibling case-study composes
# field_well_formed because it embeds the eigenboard measurement).
#
# Splinter-pole: all four discharge; page ships.
# Narcissus-pole: any sub-predicate fails; deployment blocked at the
#   failing altitude.
# Narcissus-warned: all four discharge but at least one is warned
#   (e.g., document warns deprecated anchor; design warns APCA at
#   lower bound); page ships with audit-flag.
landing_well_formed(
  state: landing_model,
  m: landing_msg,
  p: perturbation
) -> verdict
requires init_pure(p)
requires update_pure(state, m, p)
requires view_pure(state, p)
requires document_well_formed(state, p)
{ \ }

# === §9 Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. Cover image OID forward-promised. The Spectral Remix cover-image
#    content-hash + asset bytes land at Phase G via @mirror/store
#    content-addressed load. This shard substrate-decl's the cover_
#    image_ref carrier; the ACTUAL bytes attach at Phase G runtime
#    per @mirror/store discipline.
#
# 2. Corpus link resolves to Ghost.io at v0.1. The systemic.engineering
#    corpus lives at Ghost.io at v0.1 ship time; v0.2 corpus migration
#    swaps the link target to substrate-native mirror-served corpus.
#    Redirect strategy per launch.md "redirect strategy" hedge (Ghost
#    URLs → spectral.engineer equivalents via HTTP 301; DNS swap at
#    v0.2 completion).
#
# 3. cmd + sub as bare refs at v0.1. Refinement to typed effect
#    descriptions forward-promised once @io adapter species name
#    concrete effect shapes (HTTP fetch, localStorage, media-query
#    subscription, scroll listener, etc.) — same hedge inheritance
#    from @docs/tea parent hedge 4.
#
# 4. SUBSTRATE-DECL ONLY. The Gleam Lustre runtime, the actual page
#    HTML, the CSS bytes, the BEAM binary, the fly.io deployment —
#    all cascade-emission territory. This shard carries the TYPED
#    SHAPE the emission cascade discharges against. Per Alex
#    2026-08-12 no-scaffold reframe: emission runtime lives at
#    rust/src/apply_h.rs FLOOR discharge for apply_mirror_gestalt +
#    apply_gestalt_gleam (currently `{ \ }` in landed cascade
#    species; forward-promised Reed cascade this arc).
#
# 5. v0.1 minimum-landing does NOT ship the compiler-in-browser.
#    The blinking-cursor "What do you want to know?" prompt per
#    launch.md landing-page-vision section is v0.3 WASM prompting
#    surface territory. v0.1 = static landing; v0.3 = compiler on
#    the page. Per Alex 2026-08-03 Q1 minimum-landing discharge.

out @docs/tea/spectral-engineer-landing
out theme_state
out viewer_position
out landing_model
out landing_msg
out hero_layout
out footer_layout
out theme_toggle_state
out machine_metadata
out init_landing
out update_landing
out view_landing
out subscribe_landing
out landing_well_formed
